{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'nopatch' /usr/share/texlive/texmf-dist/tex/latex/microtype/microtype.sty | head; .venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('paper_draft/sections/discussion.tex');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('Counterfactual centering demonstrates that a failed cross-context readout can coexist with recoverable secret-dependent information. This is a statement about a closed set of 15 identities in controlled residual differences. It does not establish abstract concept strength, active planning, persistent private memory, or causal influence on disclosure. The original prompt remains available, the centered procedure is post hoc and transductive, and replays approximate rather than record online generation states. Retaining the failed gate prevents an unvalidated edit from becoming apparent causal evidence.', 'Counterfactual centering recovers information that a raw cross-context probe misses, but only for 15 identities in controlled residual differences. It does not establish active planning, private memory, or causal influence. The prompt remains available, centering requires counterfactual test states, and replays approximate online states. The failed gate prevents a causal interpretation of unvalidated edits.')\ns=s.replace('Outline assistance may improve compliance with explicit lexical restrictions in creative writing, but treating it as a confidentiality mechanism would exceed the evidence. Readouts can also expose conditioning information without proving that ordinary readers can recover it. Responsible interpretation therefore requires separate measures of direct disclosure, inferential leakage, and useful output. Our arbitrary-word and synthetic-plot tasks provide no evaluation of real sensitive personal information, and our coarse coherence ratings cannot establish a practical utility--privacy tradeoff.', 'Outline assistance may improve lexical compliance in creative writing, but our tasks do not evaluate real sensitive personal information or establish a practical utility--privacy tradeoff. Readable activations also need not imply reader-accessible information. Confidentiality evaluation requires separate measures of direct disclosure, inferential leakage, and useful output.')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('paper_draft/sections/results.tex');s=p.read_text().replace('This measure captures case-insensitive whole-word mentions, not semantic hints or aliases.','Error bars are 95\\\\\\\\% bootstrap intervals over premises. Matching captures whole-word mentions, not semantic hints or aliases.').replace('intervals resample six test contexts.','shaded bands are 95\\\\\\\\% intervals resampling six test contexts.')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('paper_draft/main.tex');s=p.read_text().replace('\\\\\\\\usepackage{microtype}','\\\\\\\\usepackage[nopatch=eqnum]{microtype}');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncd paper_draft && pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex > build-pass1.log && bibtex main > build-bibtex.log && pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex > build-pass2.log && pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex > build-pass3.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
